Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: JACAL
Upstream-Contact: Aubrey Jaffer <agj@alum.mit.edu>
Source: https://people.csail.mit.edu/jaffer/JACAL
Comment: The upstream tarball ships a number of files which are generated
 from other files in the same tarball.  These are stripped from the
 repackaged tarball (see Files-Excluded below) and regenerated at build
 time, or simply not used:
 .
   * "jacal.info" is produced from "jacal.texi" by makeinfo; debian/rules
     regenerates it.
   * "jacal.doc" is "nroff -man jacal.1"; Debian installs the "jacal.1"
     man page itself and has no use for the formatted copy.
   * "DOC/ratint.pdf" is typeset from "DOC/ratint.tex", which upstream
     stopped shipping as of 2a1.  The .tex source is restored by the
     Debian diff, so the PDF is redundant.
Files-Excluded:
 jacal.doc
 jacal.info*
 DOC/ratint.pdf

